<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia wage claim worries business-govt.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia wage claim worries business-govt.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Treasurer Peter Costello said on Monday small business was concerned the union movement's national wage claim would choke monetary policy if it was granted.</p>
<p>Costello told parliament a weekend Australian Chamber of Commerce and Industry survey identified the so-called living wage claim as the greatest threat to continued economic recovery.</p>
</text>
